# Online Excel Tool — Test Automation Suite

This repository contains a [Cypress](https://www.cypress.io/) end-to-end (E2E) test automation suite for **Online Excel Tool**, a web application with three distinct user roles: **Upper Management (Admin)**, **Group A**, and **Group B**. The suite uses the Page Object Model (POM) pattern to keep UI selectors and reusable actions separate from the test scenarios themselves.

## What This Suite Tests

The main spec (`OETMain.cy.js`) exercises the application end-to-end across all three roles, including:

**Upper Management (Admin)**
- Login
- Creating users and assigning them to a role (Upper Management, Group A, or Group B)
- Managing records (add, edit, delete)
- Managing sheet versions (add, edit, delete)
- Changing account password

**Group A**
- Login
- Adding records
- Changing account password / logout

**Group B**
- Login
- Adding and deleting financial value entries
- Changing account password / logout

## Repository Structure

```
Online-Excel-Tool/
├── Main Online Excel File/
│   └── OETMain.cy.js          # Main Cypress spec — runs the full test flow across all roles
├── Upper Management/
│   └── Files/
│       ├── LoginAdmin.js          # Admin login actions
│       ├── UserMenuAdmin.js       # Create/assign users to roles
│       ├── RecordAdmin.js         # Record management (edit/delete)
│       ├── SheetversionAdmin.js   # Sheet version management (add/edit/delete)
│       └── SettingAdmin.js        # Admin account settings
├── GroupA/
│   ├── ALogin.js               # Group A login
│   ├── ARecord.js              # Group A record creation
│   └── ASetting.js             # Group A account settings
└── Group B/
    ├── BSignin.js               # Group B login
    ├── BFinancialValue.js       # Group B financial value entries (add/delete)
    └── BSetting.js              # Group B account settings
```

Each role folder follows the Page Object Model: files export a class whose methods wrap the Cypress commands (`cy.get`, `.click`, `.type`, etc.) needed to interact with that part of the UI. `OETMain.cy.js` imports these classes and chains their methods together into readable test cases.
